<mujoco model="track_b_b0_single_body_placeholder">
  <!--
    B0.3 -- Minimal single-body MJCF, Track B (MuJoCo backend).

    Purpose: prove the basic MuJoCo pipeline runs at all (B0.4), before
    any calibrated physics is wired in. This file is NOT physics-accurate
    and must not be mistaken for a calibrated vehicle model.

    - freejoint: gives the body full 6-DOF free-floating motion, required
      for an AUV that is not fixed to any frame.
    - mass = 11.2 kg: matches vehicle_spec.yaml's fixed mass_kg. This is
      the one real, calibration-derived number in this file.
    - diaginertia = 0.15 0.25 0.20 kg*m^2: PLACEHOLDER ONLY. Explicit,
      finite, positive values chosen to be physically plausible for a
      body of this mass, but NOT derived from vehicle_spec.yaml or any
      calibration/optimization run. Do not treat these as real vehicle
      parameters.
    - No actuators, no hydrodynamics, no added mass, no damping, no
      buoyancy, no cross-coupling: this is a pure passive rigid body for
      B0.4's sanity run (step with zero applied force, confirm it
      behaves plausibly). B0.5/B1 is where the real calibrated physics
      (via compute_acceleration()) gets wired in -- not this file.
  -->
  <option gravity="0 0 -9.81"/>

  <worldbody>
    <body name="auv_placeholder" pos="0 0 0">
      <freejoint/>
      <!-- PLACEHOLDER inertial properties -- see file header. -->
      <inertial pos="0 0 0" mass="11.2" diaginertia="0.15 0.25 0.20"/>
      <!-- Visualization/collision geometry only. Does NOT drive mass
           properties -- the explicit <inertial> above overrides any
           geom-inferred mass/inertia. -->
      <geom type="box" size="0.3 0.15 0.15" rgba="0.2 0.5 0.8 1"/>
    </body>
  </worldbody>
</mujoco>